---
slug: admin/support/board/move
method: post
---
{%- comment -%}
  A card changed column, which means the ticket changed status.

  The same endpoint serves three callers: the drag, the card's Move to
  menu, and Undo. It does what the properties panel does to a status, so
  the change is logged the same way and shows up the same way everywhere
  else.

  Closing is asked about rather than done. Rather than a dialog the script
  opens, this sends the agent back to the board with the question on it,
  which means the keyboard and no JavaScript paths get asked too. Undo
  carries confirmed, because reverting a change is not a new decision.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Guarded twice, and the order matters. The unscoped check first, so an
    anonymous caller is sent to log in before the page looks anything up
    and before a missing ticket can tell them it is missing. The
    department scoped check once there is a ticket to scope it to.
  endcomment
  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/require_permission', do: 'support.tickets.update', entity: null
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag

  function current_profile = 'modules/user/helpers/current_profile'
  function statuses = 'modules/support/queries/statuses/search', kind: null
  function ticket = 'modules/support/queries/tickets/find', id: context.params.ticket_id, number: null

  assign return_to = context.params.return_to | default: '/admin/support/board'

  if ticket == blank
    # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
    include 'modules/support/helpers/redirect_back', url: return_to
    # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
  endif

  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/require_permission', do: 'support.tickets.update', entity: ticket
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag

  comment
    The target has to be one of this instance's statuses. The id arrives
    in a form field, so a crafted post would otherwise be able to park a
    ticket on a status that does not exist, where no column would show it.
  endcomment
  assign target = null
  assign previous = null
  for status in statuses
    if status.id == context.params.status_id
      assign target = status
    endif
    if status.id == ticket.status_id
      assign previous = status
    endif
  endfor

  if target == blank or target.id == ticket.status_id
    # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
    include 'modules/support/helpers/redirect_back', url: return_to
    # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
  endif

  assign joiner = '?'
  if return_to contains '?'
    assign joiner = '&'
  endif

  if target.kind == 'closed' and context.params.confirmed != '1'
    assign ask = return_to | append: joiner | append: 'confirm=' | append: ticket.id | append: '&to=' | append: target.id
    # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
    include 'modules/support/helpers/redirect_back', url: ask
    # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
  endif

  function stamps = 'modules/support/helpers/status/stamps', status: target

  graphql _ = 'modules/support/tickets/set_status', id: ticket.id, status_id: target.id, closed_at: stamps.closed_at, solved_at: stamps.solved_at

  assign actor_id = current_profile.user.id
  assign activity = { "ticket_id": ticket.id, "actor_id": actor_id, "action": "status_changed", "from_value": previous.name, "to_value": target.name }
  function _ = 'modules/support/commands/activities/create', object: activity

  comment
    Undo says nothing on the way back. Offering to undo the undo is a
    loop, and the agent already knows what they just did.
  endcomment
  assign done = return_to
  unless context.params.undo == '1'
    assign done = return_to | append: joiner | append: 'moved=' | append: ticket.id | append: '&from=' | append: ticket.status_id
  endunless

  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/redirect_back', url: done
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
-%}
